-- title:
--   Supersingular valuation ring with smooth-point stalks at every layer
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`.
--
--   **Data and hypotheses.** Fix a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$, an integer $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`.
--
--   *Supersingular places.* $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` $= \kappa(j_q, j_{q,M'})$ over $\kappa$, and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ`: those places $w$ which are rational (the structure map $\kappa \to w$'s residue field is surjective), which are affine geometric places, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the generator `jGeomGen κ M'` lies in `ssJSet q κ`. An element $s \in W$ is fixed.
--
--   *Reduction of $q$-expansions.* `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of subfields of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$, where the former is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field and the latter is `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2 M') (levelH q M')`. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the source, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal of those integers, compatible with $A$ on constants and with the residue map of $A$, together with a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *Small constants.* $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has image in $A$. Writing $A \cap k_0$ for `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, the hypotheses require that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), that it is a henselian local ring (`hhens`), that its residue field is algebraically closed (`hres`), and (`hκ`) that every $a \in A$ admits $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ and $a - c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   *Auxiliary constants.* $\ell$ is a prime with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ has image in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q \cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   *Layers.* $\iota$ is a type, $K : \iota \to$ intermediate fields of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with each $K_n$ finite over $k_0$, and $A_n$ is a valuation subring of $K_n$ with $x \in A_n \iff x \in A$ for $x \in K_n$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Giving `fieldBar q M'` the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`, there exist an intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'` and a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   1.
--
--   $F_0$ together with the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generates everything: `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (Set.range (algebraMap (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (fieldBar q M'))) ⊔ F₀ = ⊤`.
--
--   2.
--
--   For $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   3.
--
--   $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   4.
--
--   The image of $\pi_0$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   5.
--
--   There is $t \in W_0$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, then every coefficient of $p$ has image in $W_0$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   6.
--
--   For every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, if
--    - at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ one has $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(g)$ whenever $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$, and
--    - the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$,
--
--   then the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` under the inclusion given by `hle` lies in $F_0$, the resulting element of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that element and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   <ol start="7">
--
--   For every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ maps $F_0$ into $F_0$, and for $f \in F_0$ with image also in $F_0$, $f \in W_0$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$.
--
--   For every field $F^{ss}$ equipped with a $\kappa$-algebra structure and every `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $F^{ss}$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue map to $F^{ss}$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and with its residue map, and such that every nonzero element becomes integral with nonzero residue after scaling by a constant) such that for $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in R.\mathrm{integers} \iff f \in W_0$, both of the following hold.
--
--   (a) *Drinfeld identification of the special fibre.* For every $(\mathbb F_{q^2} =$`GaloisField q 2`$)$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e : F^{ss} \cong$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field inside the Drinfeld function field of the group generated by the $C_s$-action) such that $\#C_s = 2\,\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, and such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, granted that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and that $(\,$`redQ q γ`$, 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), the induced residual automorphism `R.resAut` of that level automorphism corresponds under $e$ to the action [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) of that element on the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   (b) *Smooth-point stalks at all layers.* There exist a finite set $N$ of places of $F^{ss}$ over $\kappa$, and, for each place $Q$ of $F^{ss}$ over $\kappa$ and each $n \in \iota$, a subring $S_{Q,n}$ of `fieldBar q M'`, a ring homomorphism $\varphi_{Q,n} : A_n[X] \to S_{Q,n}$, a ring homomorphism $\chi_{Q,n} : S_{Q,n} \to \kappa$ and a set $D_{Q,n}$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, such that $\#N = q+1$ and, for every $Q \notin N$:
--
--   for every $n$: the map $A_n \to \kappa$ sending $a$ to the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$ is surjective; the image in `fieldBar q M'` of every $a \in A_n$ lies in $S_{Q,n}$; $\varphi_{Q,n}$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a)$ equals the image of $a$ in `fieldBar q M'`; $\chi_{Q,n}(\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a))$ equals the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; $\chi_{Q,n}(\varphi_{Q,n}(X)) = 0$; for every $c \in A_n$ with residue $0$ in $\kappa$ there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi : S_{Q,n} \to A_n$ with $\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a)) = a$ for all $a \in A_n$, with residue in $\kappa$ of $\chi(f)$ equal to $\chi_{Q,n}(f)$ for all $f$, and with $\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(X)) = c$; every $f \in S_{Q,n}$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there equals the image of $\chi_{Q,n}(f)$ under $\kappa \to Q$'s residue field; $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue has $Q.\mathrm{ord}$ equal to $1$; a place $P$ lies in $D_{Q,n}$ if and only if $P$ is rational, every $f \in S_{Q,n}$ lies in $P$'s valuation subring with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for every $f \in S_{Q,n}$ the inequality $A.\mathrm{valuation}(P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)) < 1$ holds exactly when $\chi_{Q,n}(f) = 0$; $\varphi_{Q,n}(X) \neq \varphi_{Q,n}(C\,c)$ for every $c \in A_n$; $S_{Q,n}$ is a local ring whose maximal ideal is the vanishing locus of $\chi_{Q,n}$, and it is noetherian and a unique factorisation monoid; $S_{Q,n}$ is contained in the composite $L_n :=$ `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (image of K n in fieldBar q M') ⊔ F₀`, and every element of $L_n$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in S_{Q,n}$, $h \neq 0$; for every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K_n$ and every family $a$ of elements of $L_n$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; every ring homomorphism $\chi : S_{Q,n} \to A_n$ satisfying the two normalisations above has kernel the principal ideal generated by $\varphi_{Q,n}(X) - \varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(X)))$; there is a generator $\varpi$ of the maximal ideal of $A_n$, $\varpi \neq 0$, such that $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi)$ is prime in $S_{Q,n}$, such that for $f \in L_n$ one has $f \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in S_{Q,n}$ and $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi) \nmid h$, and such that for every prime $p$ of $S_{Q,n}$ not associated to $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x \in S_{Q,n}$ there is a monic polynomial $r$ over $A_n$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of $r$ pushed forward along $\varphi_{Q,n} \circ C$; and there is a finite subset $G$ of $S_{Q,n}$ such that every $f \in S_{Q,n}$ satisfies $f h = g$ with $g, h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_n$ and $h$ the image of a unit of $S_{Q,n}$;
--
--   and a compatibility block across layers: there is a proof that $K_n \le K_{n'}$ implies $S_{Q,n} \subseteq S_{Q,n'}$, and moreover for $K_n \le K_{n'}$ the ring $S_{Q,n'}$ is contained in the subring generated by $S_{Q,n}$ together with the image of $A_{n'}$; for all $n, n'$ the elements $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ and $\varphi_{Q,n'}(X)$ have the same image in `fieldBar q M'`; and for $K_n \le K_{n'}$ and $f \in S_{Q,n}$ one has $\chi_{Q,n'}(f) = \chi_{Q,n}(f)$.
--
--   Furthermore: for $Q, Q' \notin N$, if some place $P$ lies in both $D_{Q,n}$ and $D_{Q',n}$ for some $n$, then $Q = Q'$; for $Q \notin N$, every $n$ and every $P \in D_{Q,n}$ one has $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the $q$-expansion `jq`; and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, granted that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and for every place $Q$ of $F^{ss}$: the translate of $Q$ by the residual automorphism `R.resAut τ` lies in $N$ if and only if $Q$ does, and when $Q \notin N$ one has [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.smulDisc τ (Dn Q n)`](def/AlgebraicCurve_ResidueDiscs.html#L120) $= D_{\,\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q,\,n}$ for every $n$, where `smulDisc τ D` is the set of places $P$ with $\tau^{-1} \cdot P \in D$.
--
--   This is the construction, over the field of small constants $k_0$, of the supersingular valuation ring $W_0$ on the full-level modular function field together with the charts ('smooth-point stalks') $S_{Q,n}$ at every finite layer $K_n$, their sections, residue maps and residue discs, and the identification of the special fibre at a supersingular point with a quotient of the Drinfeld function field in characteristic $q$. It is obtained from the corresponding statement with an explicit bottom layer by taking that layer to be $k_0$ itself, and it feeds into [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages), where the per-layer data are assembled into the packages used in the study of the reduction of $X_H(q^2M')$ at $q$.
